From the diagram,
\(\mathrm{OA}=\mathrm{L} / \sqrt{2}\)
$\Longrightarrow \mathrm{AC}=\mathrm{BC}=\mathrm{L}\mathrm{AD}=\mathrm{L} \sqrt{2}$
Net electrical force on charge \(A\) is:
$\begin{array}{l}
\mathrm{F}=\mathrm{F}_{\mathrm{AD}}+\mathrm{F}_{\mathrm{AB}} \cos 45^{\circ}+\mathrm{F}_{\mathrm{AC}} \cos 45^{\circ} \\
\mathrm{F}=\frac{\mathrm{Q}^{2}}{4 \pi \varepsilon_{\mathrm{o}} \times 2 \mathrm{~L}^{2}}+\frac{\mathrm{Q}^{2}}{4 \pi \varepsilon_{\mathrm{o}} \mathrm{L}^{2} \sqrt{2}}+\frac{\mathrm{Q}^{2}}{4 \pi \varepsilon_{\mathrm{o}} \mathrm{L}^{2} \sqrt{2}} \\
\mathrm{~F}=\frac{\sqrt{2} \mathrm{Q}^{2}}{16 \pi \varepsilon_{\mathrm{o}} \mathrm{L}^{2}}(2 \sqrt{2}+1)
\end{array}
Perpendicular to the string, net force is zero. \(\mathrm{F} \sin 45^{\circ}=\mathrm{mg} \sin 45^{\circ}\)
$\begin{array}{l}
\frac{\sqrt{2} \mathrm{Q}^{2}}{16 \pi \varepsilon_{0} \mathrm{~L}^{2}}(2 \sqrt{2}+1)=\mathrm{mg} \\
\mathrm{Q}=1.61 \times 10^{-6} \mathrm{C}
\end{array}
